## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design end-to-end tests for asynchronous bulk import workflows in a distributed system. It probes understanding of idempotency handling, auditability, and resilience testing across multiple microservices.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing across UI, backend, and message bus
- Batch processing with idempotency and retry semantics
- Partial failure handling with deterministic retries
- Eventual consistency verification
- Test data isolation and deterministic test design

## Code Example
```javascript
// playwright/bulk-import.spec.js
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test.describe('Bulk Data Import', () => {
  test('handles 10k records with idempotency, retries, and eventual consistency', async ({ page }) => {
    // Seed test data
    await seedTestEnvironment();

    // Mock message bus for partial failure simulation
    await mockMessageBus({
      failProbability: 0.1,
      deterministicSeed: 42
    });

    // Mock downstream services
    await mockDownstreamServices();

    // Upload CSV
    const fileChooserPromise = page.waitForEvent('filechooser');
    await page.click('[data-testid="upload-button"]');
    const fileChooser = await fileChooserPromise;
    await fileChooser.setFiles('./test-data/10k-records.csv');

    // Verify progress bar updates
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="progress-bar"]')).toBeVisible();
    const progressText = page.locator('[data-testid="progress-text"]');

    // Wait for completion with 15-minute timeout
    await expect(progressText).toHaveText('100%', { timeout: 900000 });

    // Assert per-record audit logs
    const auditLogs = await fetchAuditLogs();
    expect(auditLogs).toHaveLength(10000);
    expect(auditLogs.filter(log => log.status === 'success')).toHaveLength(9000);
    expect(auditLogs.filter(log => log.status === 'retried')).toHaveLength(1000);

    // Test idempotency - re-upload same file
    await fileChooserPromise;
    await page.click('[data-testid="upload-button"]');
    const secondFile = await fileChooserPromise;
    await secondFile.setFiles('./test-data/10k-records.csv');

    // Verify no duplicates created
    const recordCount = await fetchRecordCount();
    expect(recordCount).toBe(10000);

    // Verify eventual consistency - records appear in UI and API
    await page.waitForFunction(
      () => fetchRecordCount() === 10000,
      { timeout: 300000, polling: 2000 }
    );

    // UI assertion
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="record-count"]')).toContainText('10,000');

    // API assertion
    const response = await page.request.get('/api/records');
    expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
    expect(response.json()).toHaveLength(10000);
  });
});
```

